  "notes": "Interscope/University pop-R&B: Tricky Stewart's breakout canvas plus Dru Hill and Swizz-orbit features, 1998–2003. The research gives \"78–139: half-time ballads at 78–98, straight/uptempo 100–139\", and the half-time band is encoded because the entry's only drum description belongs to it — the sourced 98 record with \"a gapped, stop-start 16th kick pattern with the snare on 3 and stabbed hat bursts\". So `halfTime` is true, the snare is `halftime_3` and the mode is 98. Three drum deltas follow: a kick at three to five hits a bar with syncopation 0.68 and a 0.3 `beatSkipProb` (that is what \"gapped, stop-start\" is), a snare on beat 3 sitting almost on the grid, and a non-continuous hat at 0.4 fill density with a high roll frequency — the \"stabbed bursts\". Harmony is \"two-chord minor-9th vamps with a plucked or bell lead\", so `maxChords` is 2 and ninth is the largest extension share. \"Light, breathy soprano-alto kept in a narrow range with rhythmic rather than melismatic phrasing; harmony stacked thin\" is a sixteen-semitone melody register with a 0.8 step share, a 3–5 pitch motif and a counter density of 0.34. The low end is \"articulated 808 sub in 16ths tuned to the vamp root, cutting out entirely on the pre-chorus\" — articulated rather than sustained, so it is the `bassline` block on `mirror_kick` with no `drums.bass808`. ⚠ The research marks that 808 description `[LOW-CONF]` and it is repeated here. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry's harmony line is \"two-chord minor-9th vamps with a plucked or bell lead\", and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\") — so weighting `vamp` at the top rendered a **one**-chord bed the research nowhere describes. The chord motion the entry states is now carried by `1_per_bar` (the pair over a 2-bar cell) and `2_bars_per_chord` (the pair over a 4-bar cell), with `vamp` kept as the minority for the held reading. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
